{"type":"standard","title":"Gina Hinojosa","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gina Hinojosa</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q28314533","titles":{"canonical":"Gina_Hinojosa","normalized":"Gina Hinojosa","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gina Hinojosa</span></span>"},"pageid":52861860,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Gina_Hinojosa_at_LBJ_Library_Forum_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/330px-Gina_Hinojosa_at_LBJ_Library_Forum_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Gina_Hinojosa_at_LBJ_Library_Forum_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":800,"height":1066},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1380358502","tid":"dd9557a0-c865-11f1-842f-dd31e543ec5d","timestamp":"2026-10-15T06:58:46Z","description":"American lawyer and politician (born 1973)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Hinojosa","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Hinojosa?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Hinojosa?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gina_Hinojosa"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Hinojosa","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Gina_Hinojosa","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Hinojosa?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gina_Hinojosa"}},"extract":"Regina Inez Hinojosa is an American lawyer and politician who is the Democratic nominee for the 2026 Texas gubernatorial election. Hinojosa is a member of the Texas House of Representatives, representing the 49th district. She is a member of the Democratic Party and was sworn into the Texas House on January 10, 2017, after winning the November 2016 general election.","extract_html":"<p><b>Regina Inez Hinojosa</b> is an American lawyer and politician who is the Democratic nominee for the 2026 Texas gubernatorial election. Hinojosa is a member of the Texas House of Representatives, representing the 49th district. She is a member of the Democratic Party and was sworn into the Texas House on January 10, 2017, after winning the November 2016 general election.</p>"}